17 2 ElectronicPollBooks. AmendRSA652:27,Itoreadasfollows:
18 I. Cities and towns are hereby authorized to use electronic poll book devices for voter
19 registration and check-in for elections, town business and deliberative sessions and special
20 meetings, and school district business and deliberative sessions and special meetings
21 provided that any city or town using electronic poll book devices shall comply with all statutes
22 directly or indirectly related to voter checklists and maintenance of the statewide centralized voter
23 registration database including the processes related to voter registration, voter check-in and check-
24 out, the processing of absentee ballots, the collection of all fields of data required for registration or
25 check-in, and the delivery of that data to the secretary of state in a format compatible with the
26 statewide centralized voter registration database. The provisions of RSA 654:34, RSA 659:55, RSA
27 659:13, RSA 659:14, and RSA 659:23, as they relate to manual entries on a paper checklist, are
28 hereby waived in order to accommodate an electronic poll book, provided the same information
29 requiredofthevoterisobtainedandrecordedbytheelectronicpollbook,andcanberetrievedand/or
30 printed at any time including during an election. In addition, nonpublic data related to individual
31 voter data shall remain confidential, and no voter data shall be released or retained by an electronic
32 poll book vendor, including its agents, or any company or individual that provides software,
