-Page2-
1 hardware, or services to the vendor for any purpose. An electronic poll book vendor shall not have
2 access to any voter data except as specifically necessary to setup, maintain, or train for an electronic
3 poll book program authorized under RSA 652:27. Adequate back-up systems shall be in place as
4 determined by the local election officials for local elections and the secretary of state for all other
5 elections. A back-up system shall include a "real time" download or accurate account of voters who
6 have checked in or registered on the day of the election. The electronic poll book shall have the
7 ability to generate a paper voter checklist completely marked to reflect participation in the election
8 up to the time of any system failure or malfunction, and sufficient number of high speed printers
9 shall be available in the polling place to produce a back-up paper checklist for use in the event of a
10 system failure, or a paper checklist shall be marked in parallel with the electronic poll book
11 reflecting the real time check-in of voters with a lag time of no more than 30 minutes. A marked
12 checklist shall be printed upon the completion of every election along with any reports required by
13 statuteandshallberetainedbytheclerk.
14 3 EffectiveDate. Thisactshalltakeeffect60daysafteritspassage.
